  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nToday, dry weather is expected for most of the area as high \npressure begins to build in behind a cold front to our south. \nIsolated showers or possibly a thunderstorm due to an inverted\nsurface trough are possible across the far southern portion of \nthe forecast area (south of a ZZV- MGW line).\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nModel ensembles indicate a strong ridge will build toward the\nUpper Ohio Valley region through the middle of the upcoming\nweek. With higher 500 mb heights, temperatures are expected to\nwarm. Wednesday is forecast to be the warmest with 500 mb \nheights approaching 594 dm. Highs by then should be in the \nlower 90s outside of the higher terrain, with heat index values \ngenerally in the mid 90s.\n\nThe ridge is forecast to weaken as a trough moves southward\nover the eastern half of the country later in the week. This \nwill result in a slight decrease in temperatures. NW flow aloft \nis then expected to develop into next weekend, with possible \ncrossing shortwaves and convection potential increasing.",
